  "id": "menopausal-depression",
  "term": "menopausal depression",
  "definition": "Menopausal depression is depression that develops during the transition from perimenopause to postmenopause. It is described as being closely associated with falling and fluctuating estrogen levels and may involve low mood along with anxiety, sleep problems, and cognitive difficulties.",
